{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794368239,"nonce":"tfokpWuyYbjuq9N/EBPovcnuPqs=","title":"perf: follow-ups to acquiring the swapchain image after the draw decision (no backoff, lost log, stale comment, restyle test)","message":"Follow-ups to the change that acquires the swapchain image after the draw decision (branch fix-acquire-after-decide, upstream PR 76). None blocks it.\n\n1. No backoff on a persistent acquire error (frame/acquire.rs, acquire_for_draw). Every failure (Lost, Outdated, Timeout, Other) marks the frame dirty and requests a redraw at once, and Lost, Outdated and Timeout also reconfigure the surface. If the error never clears, the loop retries as fast as winit delivers redraws. This may happen for a minimized window on Windows/Vulkan: lifecycle.rs ignores 0x0 resizes, and whether winit delivers redraws to a minimized window was not checked. Fix: a short delay (wake_at) or a limit on consecutive failures before the next retry.\n2. `Other` is no longer logged. The old code warned with the error; the new code maps it to a bare variant and the text is lost. Keep the wgpu error in the variant and log it.\n3. The comment above `let surf` in frame.rs (the early surface binding) still says the frame-gate recovery and the acquire use it. Both now bind the surface later, near the acquire. Reword or drop the early binding.\n4. Test coverage: class_background_survives_a_visual_only_update and class_background_survives_a_layout_changed_update pass even without the restyle, because a node whose own hash is unchanged keeps its props. Only the control test (incremental_update_alone_drops_the_class_background_of_a_replaced_node) covers the restyle path. Add a test that goes red when the restyle is removed, for a node whose props are replaced.\n\nPlanned for the fs-blinc-4 package, after the releases.","files":null}]}